=== PARITY (vs web EditableText.tsx) ===
  Data sources (web → native seams):
    useAnnouncer  → EditableTextAnnouncer seam (AccessibilityNotification.Announcement) (P1/S8)
    useTranslation → EditableTextStrings facade (P1/S10)
    useId          → SwiftUI @FocusState + the model focusRequest token (no DOM id needed)
    onSave (prop)  → EditableTextSaver async seam (the view never issues the mutation itself)
  Verbatim web logic ported + unit-pinned:
    normalise = trim · commitDraft order (next===current no-op → empty → validate → lastSubmitted
    duplicate → onSave) · handleInputChange live validation (empty not surfaced live; validator on
    trimmed) · handleInputBlur (inert while saving or invalid, else commit) · visibleText/empty-hint ·
    success → useAnnouncer "{{label}} saved" + exit · rejection → stay open, show err.message, refocus.
  States (all render, never a blank box):
    display(value) · display-empty(hint, web `placeholder` fallthrough) · edit-idle · edit-invalid
    (live + commit) · saving (web role=status "Saving…") · save-error (web ErrorText, stays open,
    refocus) · disabled · custom-display render prop.
    NOTE on the generic state template (loading/empty/error/stale/offline): EditableText is a
    CONTROLLED primitive with NO async data feed in the web spec — its only async is the in-flight
    save. The web branches map as empty→hint, error→validation/save error, loading→saving. There is
    NO stale/offline freshness axis in the web source (no query, no connection), so none is invented
    here — reproducing the source faithfully (no silent drift). The data-panel freshness envelope used
    by feature-view leaves (e.g. 0231) is deliberately absent because the web source has none.
  i18n: the 4 source keys (editableText.error.empty / .announce.saved / .error.saveFailed / .saving)
    + native a11y chrome (editableText.editHint / .editing) all resolve via the P1/S10 facade; catalog
